==English==
[[Image:Kiwifugl.jpg|thumb|right|A brown kiwi (Apteryx australis).]]
[[Image:Kiwi (Actinidia chinensis) 1 Luc Viatour.jpg|thumb|right|[[kiwi fruit|Kiwi fruit]].]]

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|mi|kiwi}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkiːwi/}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-kiwi.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːwi|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|kiwi|kiwis}}

# A [[flightless]] [[bird]] of the genus {{taxfmt|Apteryx|genus}} native to [[New Zealand]].
# {{alternative case form of|en|Kiwi||person from New Zealand}}.
# {{lb|en|informal}} A New Zealand [[dollar]].
# A [[kiwi fruit]].
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} A [[green]]-yellow [[colour]], like that of kiwi fruit flesh (also called kiwi green).
#: {{color panel|95B43F}}
# {{lb|en|military|slang}} A member of the [[air force]] who does not [[fly]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1953|title=Air Force: Official Service Journal of the U.S. Army Air Forces
|passage=And as its role grew in importance, ground commanders, or '''kiwis''' as they were called, made many mistakes in judgment {{...}}}}

====Usage notes====
* When used to describe people, ''Kiwi'' is usually capitalised.
* The plural is usually ''kiwis''; sometimes, ''kiwi'' is found as an (invariant) plural form.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|flightless bird}} {{l|en|apteryx}}
* {{sense|kiwi fruit}} {{l|en|Chinese gooseberry}} {{qualifier|dated}}, [[kiwi fruit]]

